.TH TTY 1 "FUZIX" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
tty \- print the current terminal name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tty [-s]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the terminal attached to standard input. -s suppresses output and
reports only status. Exit status is zero for a terminal and nonzero for
nonterminal input, such as a pipe.
